# Teaching Aggregate Demand and Supply Models

**Authors:** Wells, Graeme

## Abstract
The author analyzes the inflation-targeting model that underlies recent textbook expositions of the aggregate demand-aggregate supply approach used in introductory courses in macroeconomics. He shows how numerical simulations of a model with inflation inertia can be used as a tool to help students understand adjustments in response to demand and supply shocks of various kinds. (Contains 6 figures, 1 table and 4 notes.)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ872063

